  "notes": "e is the parent L/R-invariant inversion-excess (0 iff csorted; improving X drops it by 1). k is distance to the nearest true improving left cell (t>1, CCW neighbor 0 or larger). u counts tokens whose CCW neighbor is 0 or larger (not(0)=1). On improving X, token 1 cannot sit at position 0 or 1, so its bit in u is unchanged and du equals the change in the true pair count: du=-1 whenever k_new>=2 (only the swapped pair dies; new pairs can appear only at distance <=1), and du<=1 whenever k_new<=1. Thus for n<=11, phi=4*e+k+2*u drops by >=1 on a rotation if k>0 and on X if k=0; csorted uses rot_dist. Reversed runs have u=O(m) rather than a half-circle factor on all of e."
